![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

Since the `Storage` class closes the user-provided `http.Client` in its `close()` method, this behavior must be explicitly documented in the constructor to warn users against passing shared or persistent clients, in accordance with the repository's general rules.

```suggestion
  /// Methods retry failed requests using [defaultRetry] if the operation is
  /// [idempotent][], and don't retry them otherwise. Pass a `retry` argument
  /// to a method to change how that call is retried. The documentation for
  /// each method says when the operation is idempotent.
  ///
  /// Note that if a custom [client] is provided, it will be closed when
  /// [close] is called on this [Storage] instance. Avoid passing a shared or
  /// persistent client that is used elsewhere.
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. If a class or function accepts a user-provided http.Client (or a factory creating one) and closes it, this behavior must be explicitly documented to warn users against passing shared or persistent clients.
